<title>SPAIN: BoS to admit private paper as collateral as of May.</title>
<headline>BoS to admit private paper as collateral as of May.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain said on Thursday that it would admit private paper as collateral for money market operations from May.</p>
<p>At present, the central bank only accepts Bank of Spain certificates and public debt for collateral in money market operations.</p>
<p>But in a statement, the central bank said that as of May it will add liquidity against collateral of certain fixed-income and equity issues in addition.  </p>
<p>The Bank of Spain will admit all shares that form part of the IBEX-35 index, except for bank shares.</p>
<p>It will also admit matador issues</p>
<p>--Sharman Esarey, Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
